Alembic migrations for panchayat-complaint-tracker.

- Run from `api/` with `DATABASE_URL` set in the environment, e.g.:
  `DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://panchayat:panchayat@localhost:5432/panchayat uv run alembic upgrade head`
- Local Postgres is 16; production and CI are 17 — avoid 17-only syntax.
- Migrations are hand-written from `.ai/database/schema.md`'s compact DDL, never
  blindly trusted from `alembic revision --autogenerate` — see
  coding-guidelines.md § Migrations.
- `alembic check` (drift gate) only becomes meaningful once `app.db.models`
  exists (T-004); until then `env.py`'s `target_metadata` is `None`.
- Append-only enforcement (`complaint_status_history`, `complaint_edit_history`,
  `security_event`) is the application-level guard in `app/db/guard.py`
  (T-004); DB-level `REVOKE` hardening is a later, dedicated migration
  (TD-B04) once a second, non-owning application role is provisioned.
